  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#31226\", \"PowerToys#44319\", \"PowerToys#32530\"], \"answer\": \"This has been reported before. It is the \\\"Desktop composition is disabled\\\" COMException (0x80263001). Windows briefly drops desktop composition, which shows as a black screen. PowerToys, usually PowerToys Run, then crashes with this error. The past tickets say the root cause varies by machine and is often outside PowerToys, for example graphics driver problems or memory exhaustion. The fix they give is to update PowerToys to 0.96 or newer, which handles this more gracefully. Your report says 0.102.3001, which is already newer than 0.96. Because of that, I can't confirm the fix covers your case. Update your graphics drivers and Windows. If it still happens on the current version, comment on PowerToys#31226 and attach the error report or log. The log is under %LocalAppData%\\\\Microsoft\\\\PowerToys\\\\PowerToys Run\\\\Logs. Also attach a PowerToys bug report ZIP. Include your GPU and driver details, and say that it happened during a LINE voice call.\"}",
